  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact exactly as given, serialize it as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, and persist the exact bytes hashed as proposal_canon.json in the run scratch dir; then compute seed = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and verify mechanically that sha256sum proposal_canon.json equals seedHex. Re-derivation check: a third party recomputes hProposal as sha256(proposal_canon.json), then computes the final seed as sha256(hProposal + salt) (with the same salt value), and confirms it matches the provided seedHex; witness drawing is deterministic from the seed using the census rule (all 95 witnesses of census.json, in order)."
